                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "38178161",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198118124649",
                            "num_reviews": 52,
                            "playtime_forever": 119,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 119,
                            "last_played": 1512820723
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I mean... there's clearly something wrong with whoever made this game, the cringe is very real at certain points, with dubious jokes and weird visuals but you know what? The game's actually good! The puzzles are pretty easy but still require a bit of thinking and are different enough to not grow stale. The pacing is also good, alternating between slower and more frenetic moments and there's also a little adventure-like puzzle in which you have to gather some clues in order to advance. All things considered the graphics are also pretty nice and artistically inspired. I'd give this game a chance if I were you. And hey! There's also a pretty little moral lesson at the very end!\n\nIf you found this review helpful, please consider following my curator page for more: http://store.steampowered.com/curator/31397169/",
